# Build output
/zerostrike
/*.exe
dist/

# Go
*.test
*.out
coverage.html

# Project state
# .zerostrike/ is created under whatever directory is scanned (the repo
# root when running `zerostrike scan .`, but also e.g. benchmark/corpus/*
# when the benchmark tool scans each corpus case as its own root) - a
# pattern with a slash in the middle is anchored to this file's directory
# in gitignore syntax, so it must be **/-prefixed to match at any depth.
**/.zerostrike/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# docs/ is intentionally tracked (release notes, architecture docs)
# Python bytecode from scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Triage/analysis artifacts for scanned customer codebases. These quote the
# scanned application's source and file layout, so they stay local: the
# reproducible evidence lives in benchmark/corpus/fp/ instead.
/SAST-Triage-Report.md
/SAST-False-Positives-Explained.md
/false-positive-fix-goal.md
/scan-*-report*.md
